@tradition open-door
// Open door (0.60.7): end-of-shift tea on Wednesdays at the Works tea corner, where the Chief sits with whoever's
// there. It opens at 16:40; Works crew still on shift come straight from it (after-shift), Calder too.
k: 445
title: Open door
when: weekly wednesday
at: 16:40-18:00
min: 15
after-shift: yes
where: 5 room Tea corner: lounge-seat
where: 5 room Works bay: work:works, free
hold: 1
who: calder always, works 40%, tea-break 25%, everyone 4%
anim: calder talk, everyone drink
host: calder
from: calder


== mail
- Open door, Wednesday at {time}, the tea corner. Tea's on me. Questions welcome. Complaints, briefly.

== ask
- Open door at the tea corner. The Chief puts the kettle on.
- Calder does tea on Wednesdays. You can ask her anything.

== here
- She remembered my name on my second day. Still amazes me.
- Go on, ask her. She likes questions.
- Best tea in Works. Don't tell the galley.   #funny

== thanks
- End-of-shift tea in the Works corner. Chief Calder pours, listens, and remembers everything.

== chatter
- Open door later. Calder's buying. Well, pouring.   #funny
- I asked the Chief a silly question once. She answered it properly.   #warm
- Wednesday tea with the Chief. Nobody misses it.
